IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er1-rates-of-unemployment`

-- Tests of er1-rates-of-unemployment (Employment Insurance Regulations, regs 17 to 18). Piece er1.
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the Regulations (../../registers/source-bundle/SOR-96-332.txt), beside the assertion,
-- before the rule was run. The argument order is the order of the rule's GIVEN lines. A rate is a fraction (6.5% is 0.065).
-- The rates and periods below are invented to exercise the arithmetic and the edges of each period; no figure is a published rate.
-- The wrappers of reg 17.1(2) to (13) are generated from one table of hand-written expectations: for the own rate 0.06 and the
-- neighbouring rate 0.10 the five formulas give 0.09 (17.1(2)), 0.08 (17.1(4)), 0.07 (17.1(6)(a)), 0.066 (17.1(6)(b)) and
-- 0.062 (17.1(6)(c)); for own 0.10 and neighbour 0.06 each gives 0.10.
-- Calendar: 17 September 2000 was a Sunday, 3 April 2011 a Sunday (so 6 April 2011 a Wednesday and 10 April 2011 the Sunday after it).

§ `Regulation 17(4) - the monthly rates used (src:252)`

#ASSERT `reg 17(4) the seasonally adjusted monthly rates are those that incorporate the estimate for status Indians living on Indian reserves` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 17(4) the seasonally adjusted monthly rates are those that incorporate the estimate for status Indians living on Indian reserves` FALSE)

§ `Regulation 17(1) - the average of the monthly rates (src:243-246)`

-- arguments: months in the period; the rates incorporate the estimate (reg 17(4)); Statistics Canada publishes the region's rate; the monthly rates; the average Statistics Canada has determined
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the average of the seasonally adjusted monthly rates of unemployment for the period` 3 TRUE TRUE (LIST 0.04, 0.05, 0.09) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 0.06     -- (0.04 + 0.05 + 0.09) / 3
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the average of the seasonally adjusted monthly rates of unemployment for the period` 12 TRUE TRUE (LIST 0.06, 0.06, 0.06, 0.06, 0.06, 0.06, 0.08, 0.08, 0.08, 0.08, 0.08, 0.08) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 0.07     -- (0.36 + 0.48) / 12
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the average of the seasonally adjusted monthly rates of unemployment for the period` 3 TRUE TRUE (LIST 0.06, 0.07) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING        -- two rates for three months
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the average of the seasonally adjusted monthly rates of unemployment for the period` 3 FALSE TRUE (LIST 0.04, 0.05, 0.09) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING -- rates that do not incorporate the estimate of reg 17(4)
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the average of the seasonally adjusted monthly rates of unemployment for the period` 3 TRUE FALSE EMPTY (JUST 0.075) EQUALS JUST 0.075           -- not published for reasons of confidentiality: the average Statistics Canada determined
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the average of the seasonally adjusted monthly rates of unemployment for the period` 3 FALSE FALSE EMPTY (JUST 0.075) EQUALS JUST 0.075          -- reg 17(4) speaks of the monthly rates, not of the determined average
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the average of the seasonally adjusted monthly rates of unemployment for the period` 3 TRUE FALSE EMPTY NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING                  -- not published and no average determined
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the average of the seasonally adjusted monthly rates of unemployment for the period` 0 TRUE TRUE EMPTY NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING                   -- no months

-- the average once worked out: arguments: the rates incorporate the estimate (reg 17(4)); Statistics Canada publishes the region's rate; the average of the monthly rates; the average Statistics Canada determined
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the average of the monthly rates for the period, once worked out` TRUE TRUE 0.07 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 0.07
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the average of the monthly rates for the period, once worked out` FALSE TRUE 0.07 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING        -- reg 17(4) is not met
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the average of the monthly rates for the period, once worked out` TRUE FALSE 0.07 (JUST 0.075) EQUALS JUST 0.075   -- not published: the average Statistics Canada determined
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the average of the monthly rates for the period, once worked out` FALSE FALSE 0.07 (JUST 0.075) EQUALS JUST 0.075
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the average of the monthly rates for the period, once worked out` TRUE FALSE 0.07 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 17(1) - the rate for a region (src:242-246)`

-- arguments: the number of the section of Schedule I that describes the region; the three-month average; the 12-month average
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant, for a region` 2 (JUST 0.07) (JUST 0.09) EQUALS JUST 0.07     -- sections 2 to 11: the three-month average only
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant, for a region` 11 (JUST 0.07) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 0.07      -- section 11 is the last of (a); the 12-month average is not asked
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant, for a region` 12 (JUST 0.07) (JUST 0.09) EQUALS JUST 0.09   -- sections 12 to 14: the greater of the two averages
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant, for a region` 14 (JUST 0.10) (JUST 0.09) EQUALS JUST 0.10
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant, for a region` 13 (JUST 0.08) (JUST 0.08) EQUALS JUST 0.08
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant, for a region` 12 (JUST 0.07) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING      -- (b) needs both averages
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant, for a region` 13 NOTHING (JUST 0.09) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant, for a region` 2 NOTHING (JUST 0.09) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant, for a region` 1 (JUST 0.07) (JUST 0.09) EQUALS NOTHING    -- section 1 of Schedule I describes no region
#ASSERT `reg 17(1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant, for a region` 15 (JUST 0.07) (JUST 0.09) EQUALS NOTHING   -- beyond section 14

§ `Regulation 17(2) and (3) - the highest rate (src:250-251)`

#ASSERT `reg 17(2) and (3) the highest of the regional rates that apply in respect of each of those regions` (LIST 0.07, 0.09, 0.08) EQUALS JUST 0.09
#ASSERT `reg 17(2) and (3) the highest of the regional rates that apply in respect of each of those regions` (LIST 0.07) EQUALS JUST 0.07
#ASSERT `reg 17(2) and (3) the highest of the regional rates that apply in respect of each of those regions` (LIST 0.07, 0.07) EQUALS JUST 0.07
#ASSERT `reg 17(2) and (3) the highest of the regional rates that apply in respect of each of those regions` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 17(1.1) - which region's rate (src:247-251)`

-- arguments: the provision the rate is needed for; ordinarily resident outside Canada during the week; the region cannot be determined with certainty; the rates of the region or regions concerned
#ASSERT `reg 17(1.1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant` `er1 section 7 of the Act` FALSE FALSE (LIST 0.08) EQUALS JUST 0.08
#ASSERT `reg 17(1.1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant` `er1 section 7.1 of the Act` FALSE FALSE (LIST 0.08) EQUALS JUST 0.08
#ASSERT `reg 17(1.1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant` `er1 section 12 of the Act` FALSE FALSE (LIST 0.08) EQUALS JUST 0.08      -- (a) names section 12
#ASSERT `reg 17(1.1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant` `er1 section 14 of the Act` FALSE FALSE (LIST 0.08) EQUALS JUST 0.08
#ASSERT `reg 17(1.1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant` `er1 Part VIII of the Act` FALSE FALSE (LIST 0.08) EQUALS JUST 0.08
#ASSERT `reg 17(1.1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant` `er1 section 12 of the Act` TRUE FALSE (LIST 0.08) EQUALS NOTHING            -- (b) does not name section 12
#ASSERT `reg 17(1.1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant` `er1 section 14 of the Act` TRUE FALSE (LIST 0.08) EQUALS JUST 0.08
#ASSERT `reg 17(1.1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant` `er1 Part VIII of the Act` TRUE FALSE (LIST 0.08) EQUALS JUST 0.08
#ASSERT `reg 17(1.1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant` `er1 another provision of the Act` FALSE FALSE (LIST 0.08) EQUALS NOTHING    -- a provision (1.1) does not name
#ASSERT `reg 17(1.1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant` `er1 section 7 of the Act` FALSE TRUE (LIST 0.07, 0.09) EQUALS JUST 0.09       -- reg 17(2): the highest of the regions the claimant lives near
#ASSERT `reg 17(1.1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant` `er1 section 7 of the Act` TRUE TRUE (LIST 0.07, 0.09, 0.05) EQUALS JUST 0.09   -- reg 17(3): the highest of the regions the claimant was employed near
#ASSERT `reg 17(1.1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant` `er1 section 7 of the Act` FALSE FALSE (LIST 0.07, 0.09) EQUALS NOTHING         -- two rates but the region is certain: not a case the text contemplates
#ASSERT `reg 17(1.1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant` `er1 section 7 of the Act` FALSE FALSE EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 17(1.1) the regional rate of unemployment that applies to a claimant` `er1 section 7 of the Act` FALSE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 17.1 - the purposes (src:258, 263, 268, 271, 274, 284)`

#ASSERT `reg 17.1 the purpose is section 7, 7.1, 12 or 14 or Part VIII` `er1 section 7 of the Act`
#ASSERT `reg 17.1 the purpose is section 7, 7.1, 12 or 14 or Part VIII` `er1 section 7.1 of the Act`
#ASSERT `reg 17.1 the purpose is section 7, 7.1, 12 or 14 or Part VIII` `er1 section 12 of the Act`
#ASSERT `reg 17.1 the purpose is section 7, 7.1, 12 or 14 or Part VIII` `er1 section 14 of the Act`
#ASSERT `reg 17.1 the purpose is section 7, 7.1, 12 or 14 or Part VIII` `er1 Part VIII of the Act`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 17.1 the purpose is section 7, 7.1, 12 or 14 or Part VIII` `er1 another provision of the Act`)
#ASSERT `reg 17.1 the purpose is section 7, 7.1 or 14 or Part VIII` `er1 section 7 of the Act`
#ASSERT `reg 17.1 the purpose is section 7, 7.1 or 14 or Part VIII` `er1 section 7.1 of the Act`
#ASSERT `reg 17.1 the purpose is section 7, 7.1 or 14 or Part VIII` `er1 section 14 of the Act`
#ASSERT `reg 17.1 the purpose is section 7, 7.1 or 14 or Part VIII` `er1 Part VIII of the Act`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 17.1 the purpose is section 7, 7.1 or 14 or Part VIII` `er1 section 12 of the Act`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 17.1 the purpose is section 7, 7.1 or 14 or Part VIII` `er1 another provision of the Act`)

§ `Regulation 17.1(1) - the four regions (src:253-257)`

#ASSERT `reg 17.1(1) the subsection of Schedule I that describes the region` `er1 Gaspesie - Iles-de-la-Madeleine` EQUALS JUST "3(1)"
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(1) the subsection of Schedule I that describes the region` `er1 Lower St. Lawrence and North Shore` EQUALS JUST "3(11)"
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(1) the subsection of Schedule I that describes the region` `er1 Madawaska - Charlotte` EQUALS JUST "5(2)"
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(1) the subsection of Schedule I that describes the region` `er1 Restigouche - Albert` EQUALS JUST "5(3)"
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(1) the subsection of Schedule I that describes the region` `er1 a region not named in regulation 17.1` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 17.1 - the periods and the five formulas (src:258-283)`

#ASSERT `reg 17.1(2) the period from September 17, 2000 to October 6, 2001`'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2000 9 17
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(2) the period from September 17, 2000 to October 6, 2001`'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2001 10 6
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(4) the period from October 7, 2001 to October 12, 2002`'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2001 10 7
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(4) the period from October 7, 2001 to October 12, 2002`'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2002 10 12
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(6)(a) the period from October 13, 2002 to August 6, 2011`'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2002 10 13
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(6)(a) the period from October 13, 2002 to August 6, 2011`'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2011 8 6
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(6)(b) the period from August 7, 2011 to February 11, 2012`'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2011 8 7
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(6)(b) the period from August 7, 2011 to February 11, 2012`'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2012 2 11
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(6)(c) the period from February 12, 2012 to April 7, 2012`'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2012 2 12
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(6)(c) the period from February 12, 2012 to April 7, 2012`'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2012 4 7
-- arguments of each formula: the own rate; the neighbouring rate
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(2) the greater of the regional rate and the average of the neighbouring rate and the average of both rates` 0.06 0.10 EQUALS 0.09
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(2) the greater of the regional rate and the average of the neighbouring rate and the average of both rates` 0.10 0.06 EQUALS 0.10
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(4) the greater of the regional rate and the average of both rates` 0.06 0.10 EQUALS 0.08
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(4) the greater of the regional rate and the average of both rates` 0.10 0.06 EQUALS 0.10
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(6)(a) the greater of the regional rate and the average of it and the average of both rates` 0.06 0.10 EQUALS 0.07
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(6)(a) the greater of the regional rate and the average of it and the average of both rates` 0.10 0.06 EQUALS 0.10
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(6)(b) the greater of the regional rate and the sum of 85% of it and 15% of the neighbouring rate` 0.06 0.10 EQUALS 0.066
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(6)(b) the greater of the regional rate and the sum of 85% of it and 15% of the neighbouring rate` 0.10 0.06 EQUALS 0.10
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(6)(b) the greater of the regional rate and the sum of 85% of it and 15% of the neighbouring rate` 0.08 0.08 EQUALS 0.08
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(6)(c) the greater of the regional rate and the sum of 95% of it and 5% of the neighbouring rate` 0.06 0.10 EQUALS 0.062
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(6)(c) the greater of the regional rate and the sum of 95% of it and 5% of the neighbouring rate` 0.10 0.06 EQUALS 0.10


§ `Regulation 17.1(2) (src:258-262) - resident in Madawaska - Charlotte`

-- arguments: the provision the rate is needed for; the Sunday of the week of subsection 10(1); the claimant's region; the own region's subsection 17(1) rate; the neighbouring region's rate
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(2) the applicable regional rate for a claimant resident in Madawaska - Charlotte from September 17, 2000 to October 6, 2001` `er1 section 7 of the Act` (YearMonthDay 2001 1 7) `er1 Madawaska - Charlotte` 0.06 0.10 EQUALS JUST 0.09     -- inside the period: greater of 0.06 and avg(0.10, avg(0.10, 0.06)) = 0.09
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(2) the applicable regional rate for a claimant resident in Madawaska - Charlotte from September 17, 2000 to October 6, 2001` `er1 section 7 of the Act` (YearMonthDay 2000 9 17) `er1 Madawaska - Charlotte` 0.06 0.10 EQUALS JUST 0.09     -- the first day of the period: greater of 0.06 and avg(0.10, avg(0.10, 0.06)) = 0.09
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(2) the applicable regional rate for a claimant resident in Madawaska - Charlotte from September 17, 2000 to October 6, 2001` `er1 section 7 of the Act` (YearMonthDay 2001 10 6) `er1 Madawaska - Charlotte` 0.06 0.10 EQUALS JUST 0.09     -- the last day of the period: greater of 0.06 and avg(0.10, avg(0.10, 0.06)) = 0.09
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(2) the applicable regional rate for a claimant resident in Madawaska - Charlotte from September 17, 2000 to October 6, 2001` `er1 section 7 of the Act` (YearMonthDay 2001 1 7) `er1 Madawaska - Charlotte` 0.10 0.06 EQUALS JUST 0.10     -- the own rate is the greater: 0.10 against avg(0.06, avg(0.06, 0.10)) = 0.07
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(2) the applicable regional rate for a claimant resident in Madawaska - Charlotte from September 17, 2000 to October 6, 2001` `er1 section 7 of the Act` (YearMonthDay 2000 9 16) `er1 Madawaska - Charlotte` 0.06 0.10 EQUALS NOTHING     -- the day before the period
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(2) the applicable regional rate for a claimant resident in Madawaska - Charlotte from September 17, 2000 to October 6, 2001` `er1 section 7 of the Act` (YearMonthDay 2001 10 7) `er1 Madawaska - Charlotte` 0.06 0.10 EQUALS NOTHING     -- the day after the period
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(2) the applicable regional rate for a claimant resident in Madawaska - Charlotte from September 17, 2000 to October 6, 2001` `er1 section 7 of the Act` (YearMonthDay 2001 1 7) `er1 Restigouche - Albert` 0.06 0.10 EQUALS NOTHING     -- the claimant is in the neighbouring region, not this one
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(2) the applicable regional rate for a claimant resident in Madawaska - Charlotte from September 17, 2000 to October 6, 2001` `er1 another provision of the Act` (YearMonthDay 2001 1 7) `er1 Madawaska - Charlotte` 0.06 0.10 EQUALS NOTHING     -- a provision the subsection does not name
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(2) the applicable regional rate for a claimant resident in Madawaska - Charlotte from September 17, 2000 to October 6, 2001` `er1 Part VIII of the Act` (YearMonthDay 2001 1 7) `er1 Madawaska - Charlotte` 0.06 0.10 EQUALS JUST 0.09     -- Part VIII is named
#ASSERT `reg 17.1(2) the applicable regional rate for a claimant resident in Madawaska - Charlotte from September 17, 2000 to October 6, 2001` `er1 section 12 of the Act` (YearMonthDay 2001 1 7) `er1 Madawaska - Charlotte` 0.06 0.10 EQUALS JUST 0.09     -- section 12 is named for a claimant resident in the region

